Task: Fix Settings dismissal behavior on iOS.

CURRENT PROBLEM

The Settings sheet is closing too easily.

Right now, tapping different controls inside Settings or closing a child selector can dismiss the entire Settings sheet and send the user back to the chat.

This is wrong.

====================================================
EXPECTED BEHAVIOR
====================================================

The main Settings sheet may be dismissed in ONLY TWO ways:

1. Tap the main Settings X button at the top.
2. Drag/swipe the Settings sheet downward manually to dismiss it.

THAT'S IT.

No other tap, button, selector, child popup, or internal action may dismiss the main Settings sheet.

====================================================
VERY IMPORTANT
====================================================

Examples:

- Open Appearance
- choose Dark / Light / System
→ Settings must remain open.

- Open App Accent Color
- choose a color
→ Settings must remain open.

- Open Chat Color
- choose a color
→ Settings must remain open.

- Open any child popup
- press the child popup X
→ ONLY the child popup closes.
→ The main Settings sheet stays exactly where it was.

- Tap Change Email
- return from that sub-flow
→ return to Settings, not Chat.

- Tap any normal Settings row
→ do NOT dismiss Settings unless that specific action intentionally navigates away.

====================================================
MAIN SETTINGS DISMISSAL
====================================================

The MAIN Settings sheet can close only from:

A. Main Settings top X

OR

B. Native downward drag gesture on the Settings sheet

No backdrop tap dismissal.
No accidental outside-tap dismissal.
No child-modal close event dismissing the parent.
No row tap dismissing the parent.

====================================================
AFTER SETTINGS CLOSES
====================================================

This is also important:

When the user closes the MAIN Settings sheet:

DO NOT automatically send them to the Chat screen.

The Settings sheet was opened from inside the menu/drawer.

After Settings closes, the user should remain in that underlying menu/drawer state.

In other words:

Menu open
→ open Settings
→ close Settings
→ return to Menu

NOT:

Menu open
→ Settings
→ close Settings
→ Chat

The user decides when to leave the menu.

====================================================
CHILD POPUPS / SUBVIEWS
====================================================

Treat child UI independently.

Examples:
- Appearance selector
- App Accent Color selector
- Chat Color selector
- Language flow if applicable
- any future Settings child popup

Closing a child:
→ closes ONLY child
→ parent Settings stays open

Do not reuse one global "close" event for both child and parent.

Audit event propagation.

====================================================
ROOT CAUSE AUDIT
====================================================

Please inspect:

- backdrop click handlers
- event bubbling/propagation
- shared onClose handlers
- parent/child modal state
- router/navigation callbacks
- gesture dismiss handlers
- native bridge callbacks
- React state synchronization

Do not patch this with random preventDefault calls only.

Find why child actions are currently dismissing the parent Settings sheet.

====================================================
GESTURE BEHAVIOR
====================================================

The downward drag to dismiss Settings should feel native.

Important:
- only intentional downward swipe should dismiss
- normal scrolling inside Settings should NOT accidentally dismiss it
- vertical scroll and sheet-dismiss gesture must not fight each other

If Settings content is scrolled down, scrolling content should remain normal.

The sheet should dismiss only when the user intentionally drags the sheet itself downward from the appropriate state.

====================================================
DO NOT CHANGE
====================================================

Do not redesign:
- Settings UI
- Settings background
- cards
- colors
- icons
- selectors
- buttons

This task is ONLY dismissal/navigation behavior.

